WEBVTT

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:17.280
Unforgivable. Astral, Yuma...

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.800
To think they put me into this miserable state...!

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.280
But I won't let things end like this!

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.310
If the legend is true...

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.770
...straight ahead has to be...

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.220
That is...

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.340
...the place where the Barian God, Don Thousand, sleeps!

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.340
Great Don Thousand, I will offer my life to you!

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.710
So give me your power!

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.250
What is... What's going on?

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.940
Righto! Today I will jump the 20 boxes!

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.110
I'm gonna bring it-

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.710
Ow, ow...!
 Hey, are you all right?

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.510
Geez, you really <i>are</i> an idiot...

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.020
Huh?! What was that just now?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.650
What... is with that feeling...?

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.820
You are...

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.820
My name is Don Thousand.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:31.480
Thou, who donated thy life to me, what is thy wish?

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.880
Don Thousand, there's someone I want to utterly crush by all means!

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.650
Astral.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.940
Yes, and Yuma Tsukumo.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.620
Don Thousand, give me power!

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.820
Then you will need the Seven Numbers buried within the Earth.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.620
Search for these sealed Numbers!

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.080
Sealed Numbers?

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:59.340
Right. Then my power can be restored.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.820
Interesting. As long as I can defeat those guys,
I am willing to do anything!

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.770
So, give me the power!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.280
Fine.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.480
My power now lives on in thy heart.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:30.910
With this, me and thou art one body and one soul.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:20.610
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.660
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:31.120
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.670
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:39.550
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:45.890
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.100
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.980
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:56.610
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.690
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:08.160
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:33.640
"Restart the Airship!
 Aim for the Legendary Numbers!"

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.570
That memory just now... what on earth?!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.030
This is...?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.870
Just what is going on?!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.130
This sudden change in pressure...! Is it the sign of our destruction?!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.420
Exactly.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.750
Vector?!

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.630
Astral's power will be awakening soon.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.180
You bastard! How dare you come back after that disgrace?!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.520
What's that?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.390
Are you trying to say that the failure of the Sargasso strategy was all my fault?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.650
Isn't that the case?

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:24.530
Because of you, Astral and Yuma have awakened to a new level!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.740
So what?!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:31.280
You no good idiots can't even come up with a good plan on your own,

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.240
and you try to act like you're <i>superior</i> to me?

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.410
You bastard! I'll turn you into <i>food</i> for my Galaxy-Eyes!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.750
Stop it, Misael.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.210
You guys should be aware of this.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.960
That thousands of Years ago, the God of Barian World, Don Thousand,

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.470
was defeated by Astral and sealed in the darkness.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.350
Astral’s power is very strong.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:58.350
Right now, he is still absorbing Numbers, but once he regains his original power,

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.730
the Barian World will be <i>destroyed</i>.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:04.520
There you go! I've got some critical information up my sleeve.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:05.730
What do you mean?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.320
In those guys’ world, there are seven powerful Numbers that they haven't found yet.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:15.080
Let’s find them and make that power ours!

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.580
Seven Numbers, you say?

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.960
What's with that filthy fly?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:23.670
What are you saying?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.500
I am not filthy, not at all!

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.670
Ah, so itchy, itchy, itchy, itchy, itchy, <i>itchy, itchy, itchy...</i>

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.140
I revived this guy from the “Ocean of Ill Will.”

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.140
This guy's true identity is that <i>Heart Burning</i>!

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.520
Hey, that’s <i>my</i> personal catchphrase!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.520
Spitting your catchphrase in <i>this</i> form, <i>Mr. Heartland</i>?

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.440
You want to hear it?

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.280
Heart Bur- Ah, so itchy, itchy, itchy, <i>itchy, itchy, itchy...</i>

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.150
This guy knows something about the Numbers.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.950
I have seen it with my own eyes.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.950
The information about Kazuma Tsukumo inside Dr. Faker’s lab!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.250
Before he opened the door to the Parallel Worlds,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.580
he explored a total of 23 ruins.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.590
That's where the ultimate seven Numbers ought to be.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.670
If his story is true...

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.840
...we have to get them before Astral can absorb them.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.220
And besides...

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:20.560
...when we go to their world, we might find some clues about Nasch, huh?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.520
Nasch?!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:27.650
We originally consisted of seven. The Seven Emperors of Barian.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:32.780
But one day, Nasch and Merag disappeared from this world.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.910
There might be a chance that they are in their world.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.410
Very well.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.410
Durbe!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.210
We will split up to look for the Numbers.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:52.720
And now for you two sleepy-heads...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.550
With the power of Don Thousand,

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:58.550
you two shall be revived.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.970
Remember it! Alit! Gilag!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.520
The humiliation of loosing to Yuma Tsukumo!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:09.110
Vector, their recovery still needs time.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.530
Let's go ahead with the other business first.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.320
All right.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.330
Can you sense anything?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.580
No.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.590
I sensed something quite powerful moments ago, but now it's gone.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.300
Shark-sis, so your antenna's also useless?

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.220
<i>Don't </i>call me by that name!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.340
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.430
But did everyone sense the same thing at the same time?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.350
What the...?

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.240
Th- this...

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:03.790
Astral! What... Why are we in the airship?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.790
Wh-What's the deal out of the blue? You scared me!

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.920
I am sorry. But I want you to have a look at this.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.170
Just now, all of a sudden, this map with marks on several places has appeared.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.010
All seven points on the map indicate locations of ruins,

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.470
and all of those locations have Numbers.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.100
Numbers?!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.640
And this appeared along with the map.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.860
<i>Yuma. Astral.</i>

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.900
D-Dad!

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:44.330
<i>When you receive this message,
the situation is developing to the worst.</i>

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.330
<i>Head off to find the seven Numbers in the ruins as soon as possible.</i>

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.130
<i>These are special Numbers.</i>

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:56.050
<i>If they fall into the Barian’s hands, then their overwhelming power will be awakened.</i>

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:01.720
<i>Yuma, Astral, don't ever pass the Numbers to the Barians.</i>

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.300
<i>I am counting on you!</i>

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.350
Dad!

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.730
Then Dad knew about the Numbers all this time?

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.610
Right, about me too...

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.690
Yes. Dad has foreseen everything right from the start.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.450
Dad has always been guiding me.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.320
That's why I believe I have to go!

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.580
Right. We have no reason to give the Barians such power!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.950
I will go too!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.660
Shark!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.290
When Ryouga decides on something, he won’t listen to other people.

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.210
Then I will go as well!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.510
Then it’s settled, Yuma! Let’s get going!

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.760
Guys...

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.260
Alrighty! Let's set out for the Numbers!

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.510
We're gonna bring it to 'em!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.400
<i>Nasch...</i>

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.440
<i>At times like this... if you were here...</i>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.790
Somehow it feels very stormy...

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.620
Yeah...

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.040
Is this some sort of influence of the Parallel Worlds...?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.380
Umm, Astral...

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.220
Just what kind of place is the Astral World?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.970
Why are you asking that?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.550
I mean, Dad even knows about the Numbers,

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.720
so he must be in the Astral World.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:33.270
The Astral World is a place that only
those with ranked-up souls can reach.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.270
Rank-Up of souls?

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.570
Is it like when we see the Rank-Up of Monsters?

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:42.860
The souls of all living things are always aiming toward their ideals,

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.030
and this is why anyone has the possibility to Rank-Up.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.620
The- then, what would I have to do to Rank-Up as well?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.540
I don't know about that.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:57.000
But then... does this mean that you're Ranked-Up compared to me?

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.670
I don't really get that.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:03.590
Oh my, I guess there is no doubt that Astral is Ranked-Up compared to Yuma!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.720
That's right, huh?

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.890
Yuma's only special skill is shoveling food
 down fast and crapping it right-

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.060
Ko-Kotori-<i>san</i>!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.060
Geez! What are you making me say?!

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.640
You said it yourself!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.360
Stupid. There's no way for any of you to Rank-Up in your life.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.280
What’s that?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.640
Damn... The Barian Lapis is...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.730
Now I can’t even use my original power.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.350
I should have known that...

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.270
What's more, that was Astral's airship for sure!

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.150
Does this mean they are nearby-

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.540
<i>Th-This guy is...</i>

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.330
Wanna go, ya jerk?!

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.210
<i>Astral...</i>

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:41.520
That guy was so afraid he ran away from me...

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.440
Hey! Are you okay?

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:46.820
Wait, Yuma!

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.450
Keep away from that guy! You're careless!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.950
<i>Ryouga Kamishiro...</i>

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.080
Shark!?

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.620
Do you know who this guy is?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.500
O-oh... I don’t have a clue. But it seems he was injured...

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.920
That's fishy.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.920
We have clashed with an unknown energy form
in the different dimension space.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.920
If that was a Barian, then this guy...

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.590
My name is Nasch. I am just a tourist.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.390
A tourist, huh? In the wild mountains like this?

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.640
It is a bit unnatural, so be careful.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.100
Hey, wait a minute, you guys...

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.860
You... How many times do you want to get fooled?

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.150
Will you stop trusting people so easily?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.820
I know... I do know that. I...

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.240
I just...

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.320
Yuma...

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:34.950
This voice is...

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:46.210
Thi- this is...!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.050
... the ruin we were searching for!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.300
Then there's a Number inside!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:59.270
<i>No way... They are searching for Numbers just like us.</i>

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:01.810
Yuma!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.440
Kotori!

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.570
Kotori! Kotori!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.620
This...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.120
<i>Somewhere in this ruin must be a Number, </i>

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:22.040
<i>but I can’t Duel in this condition.</i>

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.000
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.880
Geez, you guys really need looking after.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.420
That’s because snakes are the archenemies of birds like me!

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:36.090
Oh! Astral, I can still see you
even though we're outside your airship!

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.350
Does that mean I've also Ranked-Up?

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.930
Why are you so carefree?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.020
This seems to be a dead end.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.190
Re... really?!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:48.860
What?!

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.940
Huh?! What’s happening?!

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:54.990
The exit was...!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:02.450
Rio, get out of the way! There's no telling what will happen next!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:07.580
Ryouga!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:12.550
Hey, Shark! Shark!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.920
I'm all right!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.340
But what’s with these mechanisms...?

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.650
Shark, a passage towards the inside has appeared!

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.770
Yes, here as well!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:31.440
It seems we have to split and move forward.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:35.400
That guy’s name is Nasch, right?

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.780
Yeah, he seems to be a tourist who's just around here,

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:43.120
but Shark and Astral suspect that he's a Barian.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.460
Huh? A Barian?

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:49.080
Umm, but I... think that's wrong.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.210
But, if he <i>is</i> a Barian, he must be
searching for Numbers as well...

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:59.470
Anyway, thanks for that a moment ago.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.310
But don't get me wrong.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.730
That doesn't mean I would trust you.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:10.190
Doesn't matter. It’s merely a return to your friend for saving me.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.820
You don't you say.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.780
What’s with this room? Is it a dead end?

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:27.290
So we got ourselves stuck good in a trap?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.330
Wha- what?!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.630
What’s with this place?

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.050
Yuma, take a look at that!

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:43.470
That's... That's the Number of this ruin?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:54.150
You... you are...?

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:59.990
I am the Guardian who protects this ruin's Number, Mach.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.450
You are the Number's guardian?

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.330
It seems like he is a spirit of a Number.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:07.330
A spirit?

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.870
I sense a strong spiritual energy from him.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.380
I cannot just hand this Number to you.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.380
If you want to own this Number,

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:21.180
I have to test the worthiness of your souls.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.300
How could I run away from the challenge to a Duel?!

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.520
Duel Disk, set!

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:31.940
D-Gazer, set!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.070
Duel!!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.990
Yuma! Do your best!

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.950
Then let's start the Duel of your trial.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.080
My turn! Draw!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.290
I set one Monster in face-down Defense Position.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.750
Then I set two cards from my hand,

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.630
and end end my turn!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.760
Here goes! My turn! draw!

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.180
Be careful, Yuma. Your opponent isn't someone ordinary.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.010
Got it.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.140
Here is the resting-place of noble souls.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.930
If you cannot pass the trial,

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.440
I shall receive <i>their</i> souls as the price.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:14.730
Their?!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.570
Shark! And Nasch!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.580
The walls are moving!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.040
Are we going to get squashed by the walls??

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.630
Ryouga!

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.220
That's low, you jerk! Let them both go!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.130
That depends on you.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.390
Within this Duel, what will you find?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.470
<i>What will we find?</i>

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.520
<i>Is the way to save these two hidden in the Duel?</i>

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.520
If that’s the case, I shall defeat you!

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:59.900
I'll absolutely save Shark and the others!

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.030
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.290
Then, when there is a Gagaga Monster on the field,

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.540
I can Special Summon this guy!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.960
Come! Gagaga Kid!

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:19.040
Then Gagaga Kid's effect activates!

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.340
When this guy is Special Summoned,

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:24.720
he can change his level to that of one other Monster on the field!

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.590
Gagaga Magician is a Level Four!

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.470
Thus his level is changed from two to four!

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:33.020
Now I have two Level Four Monsters!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:33.560
Yuma...!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:36.940
I know! If I Summon Hope using Gagaga Kid as Material,

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.650
I can't attack this turn.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:42.360
That's why I activate the Magic Card, Gagaga Tag!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.280
With the effect of this card,

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:47.110
Gagaga Monsters gain 500 Attack Points!

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.620
<i>I see. He plans to attack the opponent with both Monsters,</i>

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.700
<i>and summon Hope during the end of his turn?</i>

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.370
<i>The tactics aren't bad, but...</i>

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:58.580
<i>...something is hiding in this Duel.</i>

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:07.130
Shark! Nasch! I'll definitely save you!

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.110
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:26.650
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:27.860
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.280
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:34.660
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:37.210
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.290
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:39.330
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.710
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.050
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:48.170
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.390
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:53.390
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.350
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:56.730
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.600
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:02.900
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:07.990
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.240
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:13.240
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:18.620
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.960
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.340
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:45.520
The spirit of the Number, Mach’s insurmountable tactics are driving us into a corner.

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:48.530
And Shark and Nasch are in a pinch too.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:50.780
How can we save Shark?

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.950
So that’s the Number in the ruin!

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:56.530
The hero who rides the Pegasus... There is a hint in that legend!

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.700
Nasch... You are...?

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:04.500
"A Recollection from the Past:
 Durbe and the White Horse - a Legendary Phantom"

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:08.420
If we can’t deconstruct his combo, we will lose for sure!
